 2. Compute exp(x)
 3. Computw the natural log, log10, and log2 of a value
 4. Compute log(x, base) with a custom base
 5. Compute pow(x, y) - built-in vs mathy.pow
 """)
 choice = safe_input("Enter your choice: ").strip()

 if choice == "1":
 print("f\nmath.e = {math.exp(x)}")

 elif choice == "2":
 x= get_float(" Enter x: ")
 print(f"\nexp({x}) = e^{x} = {math.exp(x)}")

 elif choice == "3":
 x= get_float("Enter a positive number x: ")

 try:
 print(f"\n log({x}) = {math.log(x)} (natural log, base e))
 print(f" log10({x}) = {math.log10(x)})
 print(f" log2({x}) = {math.log2(x)})
 except ValueError:
